  "content_elements": [
    {
      "_id": "FRHZR3A4T5FGRL6T4KG7A667UQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "MONROE, La. (KNOE) - Voters all across the U.S. will go to the polls on Nov. 3 for the 2026 midterm elections. Here is a look at what voters will be deciding in both Louisiana and Arkansas. You can get election results <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-results/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-results/\">here</a>, and also learn more about what is on your ballot <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-coverage/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-coverage/\">here</a>. ",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "PVLKFSEMTVFL5AOQTFU74YURIQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Louisiana",
      "level": 2,
      "type": "header"
    },
    {
      "_id": "DIMIG5EVJFC5XBSXXMECUM7JFQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "In Louisiana, voters will decide on congressional races, including the open 5th congressional race and U.S. Senate. There are also ten constitutional amendments, which you can learn about <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/10/14/louisiana-voters-face-10-constitutional-amendments-november-heres-what-yes-or-no-vote-means/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/10/14/louisiana-voters-face-10-constitutional-amendments-november-heres-what-yes-or-no-vote-means/\">here</a>.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "LQODILG6J5FIDKSGMQXQSSNRCE",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Early voting runs from Oct. 20-27, except on Oct. 25. For more details, click <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/10/16/early-voting-louisiana-begins-tuesday-november-election-heres-what-know/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/10/16/early-voting-louisiana-begins-tuesday-november-election-heres-what-know/\">here</a>.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "GIRBQB5EIRDYVLZDOBYNV7LIRY",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Polls are open from 6 a.m. to 8 p.m. on Election Day, and if you are in line to vote by 8 p.m., but haven’t voted yet, you are still allowed to vote. ",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6U2LFLME6FH73HX44CIBWJ7XSA",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "To vote in person, you will need one of the following:",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "KDW3XAOUHBFZBPOWCODMJ323C4",
      "items": [
        {
          "_id": "AS5VL265PBBVDCGGTMLAUFGYXU",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "a driver’s license;",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "HRCXXPGDKVDKLCER6N3MOGZ2KU",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "a Louisiana Special ID;",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "P6XEPPCEHZHF5DN5PLPSZ3J4BE",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "LA Wallet digital driver’s&nbsp;license;&nbsp;",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "RMMOV5M43JG5JNMQYUJBHVBFCQ",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "a United States military identification card that contains your name and picture; or",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "XZTLFN3L2FBKJKRYYMM6YNFGY4",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "some other generally recognized picture ID that contains your name and signature.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "list_type": "unordered",
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "_id": "RB2CFYEUF5BV7BU67NAVDXL3DI",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "The deadline to request an absentee ballot is Oct. 30 by 4:30 p.m You can request an absentee ballot online through the state’s <a href=\"https://voterportal.sos.la.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voter Portal (opens in a new tab)\">Voter Portal</a> or in writing through the <a href=\"https://voterportal.sos.la.gov/registrar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Registrar of Voters (opens in a new tab)\">Registrar of Voters</a> Office. The deadline for the registrar of voters to receive the ballot is Monday, Nov. 2 by 4:30 p.m.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "354NJDCPWNDT5EXQ7EA5Y3DPFA",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "To see what is on your ballot click <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/08/06/candidate-qualifying-begins-november-election/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/2026/08/06/candidate-qualifying-begins-november-election/\">here</a>, or visit the Louisiana Secretary of State’s office <a href=\"https://voterportal.sos.la.gov/Home/VoterLogin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://voterportal.sos.la.gov/Home/VoterLogin\">GeauxVote portal</a>. ",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4OMS2E6ZP5BZVITOIIB5LHOKZU",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "To read election coverage leading up to the election, click <a href=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-coverage/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.knoe.com/politics/election-coverage/\">here</a>. ",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "SZGYJNVQ2ZCZRD4GQPNOFY3OY4",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Arkansas",
      "level": 2,
      "type": "header"
    },
    {
      "_id": "SO6OBOHCXNAZJB7O4ASXIUA6YA",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Arkansas voters will not only vote for U.S. Senate and congressional races but also statewide races, including governor, lieutenant governor, secretary of state, attorney general, state auditor, treasurer and commissioner of state lands. Voters will also vote for state senators and state House members. There are also four statewide amendments.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "YWHU6ZN6XVGZZPUIML76MZ7WMY",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "<a href=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._1_HJR_1018_of_2026_.pdf_.pdf\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._1_HJR_1018_of_2026_.pdf_.pdf\"><b>Issue No. 1</b></a> - Popular Name: <i>Citizenship Voting</i>",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "UXMDPF3H2FGUHJAKZDA6QJILTI",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Provide that “Only a citizen of the United States ... may vote in an election in this state”",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "YK3MROFU6NHVNKY74FYQGFG2JI",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "<a href=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._2_SJR_11_of_2026_.pdf\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._2_SJR_11_of_2026_.pdf\"><b>Issue No. 2</b></a> - Popular Name:<i> Constitutional Rights: Firearms</i>",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4QWEQW2IQRBXJEP6LIBMZFZRKY",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Provide that the right to keep and bear arms is “a natural, fundamental, and individual right that shall not be infringed”",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "DP73FPFF75CY5ELMSHTPQZN7BU",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "<a href=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._3_SJR_15_of_2026_.pdf\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._3_SJR_15_of_2026_.pdf\"><b>Issue No. 3</b></a> - Popular Name: <i>Local Government: Economic Investment</i>",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "NG5F3DEUUVECVIUML5MRSELKYU",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Allow the legislature to create programs, including Economic Development Districts, and make loans and grants of public money to develop the state economy",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7GAWEWSNCNAGTL7ZSM7U6D46ZI",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "<a href=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._4_Act_578_of_2026_.pdf\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sos.arkansas.gov/uploads/elections/Issue_No._4_Act_578_of_2026_.pdf\"><b>Issue No. 4</b></a><b> </b>- Popular Name: Flood infrastructure, storm infrastructure; Irrigation; Sewage and stormwater; Pollution; Parks and conservations - Bonds",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "BKHWGHTCBZE27GVXZHBB3E7LA4",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Federal races",
      "level": 4,
      "type": "header"
    },
    {
      "_id": "XFJSL4UEW5CDBMNHHVMZDCNTPQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "U.S. Senate - <a href=\"https://tomcotton.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://tomcotton.com/\">Tom Cotton</a> (R), <a href=\"https://www.hallieshoffner.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.hallieshoffner.com/\">Hallie Shoffner </a>(D), <a href=\"https://www.jeffwadlin.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.jeffwadlin.com/\">Jeff Wadlin</a> (L)",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "TM2DMJKHYFHQRMMOLKW5MWQZCQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "U.S. Rep. District 1- <a href=\"https://www.meetrickcrawford.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.meetrickcrawford.com/\">Rep. Rick Crawford</a> (R), <a href=\"https://www.terrigreenforarkansas.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.terrigreenforarkansas.com/\">Terri Yarbrough Green</a> (D), <a href=\"https://www.steveparsonslibertarian.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.steveparsonslibertarian.com/\">Steve Parsons</a> (L)",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "TZJ2YBGPOVDNLGWJHP6FYWDIUQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "U.S. Rep. District 4 - <a href=\"https://www.brucewesterman.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.brucewesterman.com/\">Rep. Bruce Westerman</a> (R), <a href=\"https://russellforar.com/\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://russellforar.com/\">James Russell </a>(D)",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "YTY3EMHPRZDJDLXI3CTGIR2J7M",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Statewide races",
      "level": 4,
      "type": "header"
    },
    {
      "_id": "ZW22ZXSCLRGQ3IWG6BODQSOU3E",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Several state executive races are on the ballot:",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "JY3IAP3XOJCGRLEEPUP7D7GI5A",
      "items": [
        {
          "_id": "GL7PASNBDRFMDK26GO3JRCYKEU",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "Governor - <a href=\"https://www.sarahforgovernor.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sarahforgovernor.com/\">Gov. Sarah Huckabee Sanders</a> (R), <a href=\"https://www.fredlove.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.fredlove.com/\">Fredrick Love</a> (D), <a href=\"https://www.colt4arkansas.org/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.colt4arkansas.org/\">Colt Shelby</a> (L)",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "CVX67BOYMJERTKQN25ZD7GEFJI",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "Lt. Governor - <a href=\"https://www.leslierutledge.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.leslierutledge.com/\">Lt. Gov. Leslie Rutledge</a> (R), <a href=\"https://mk4ar.org/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://mk4ar.org/\">Michael Kalagia</a>s (L)",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "E45OXDEOGRG3XE42AUFAFW2N5E",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "Secretary of State - <a href=\"https://www.kellygrappe.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.kellygrappe.com/\">Kelly Grappe</a> (D), <a href=\"https://www.hammerforarkansas.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.hammerforarkansas.com/\">Kim Hammer</a> (R), <a href=\"https://pakko4ar.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://pakko4ar.com/\">Michael Pakko</a> (L)",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "_id": "SODDI7HEI5FYNDQLFVT4DS2FUY",
          "additional_properties": {
            "indent": 0
          },
          "alignment": "left",
          "content": "Commissioner of State Lands - <a href=\"https://coleforcommissioner.com/\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://coleforcommissioner.com/\">Cole Jester</a> (R), Christopher Olson (L)",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "list_type": "unordered",
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "_id": "TOXPOMJYZRE7LPHHK4CDTVHLRM",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "Early voting begins Oct. 19 for the Nov. 3 general election. According to Arkansas law, early voting goes from 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. Monday through Friday and from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. on Saturdays, and ending at 5 p.m. on the day before the election.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "UUCLSXKQ4FESZP35X54RDNBT24",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "People can also check their voter registration, sample ballots and polling places by<b> </b><a href=\"https://www.voterview.ar-nova.org/voterview\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.voterview.ar-nova.org/voterview\"><b>going to the VoterView page</b></a> on the Secretary of State’s website.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "_id": "TZFWKMP6XNEA5IUXB4B7ZSBUDU",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "_id": "DNDQNR4DZZCGHF256KLTYB4URQ",
      "additional_properties": {},
      "content": "KNOE’s sister station KAIT in Jonesboro, Arkansas helped with this coverage. ",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
